WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.687
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Sunday, November fifteenth.

2
00:00:04.687 --> 00:00:12.225
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:14.690
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:27.031
Today: new Iranian drone attacks on Bahrain, more Houthi missiles toward Riyadh, death sentences in Jordan's church attack case, a state of emergency in Guatemala, and a deadly clash in northwest Nigeria.

5
00:00:27.031 --> 00:00:28.539
We start with Bahrain.

6
00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:35.412
Reuters reports Bahrain intercepted Iranian aerial attacks this morning as Tehran said it attacked a U.S. base.

7
00:00:35.412 --> 00:00:45.367
Radio Free Europe reports sirens and blasts were heard across the kingdom, and Iran's Revolutionary Guards claim six drones targeted a U.S. radar system at the Riffa base.

8
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:50.304
It is the second Iranian attack claim against U.S. assets in Bahrain in three days.

9
00:00:50.304 --> 00:00:57.099
Separately, A F P reports Iran's navy and Revolutionary Guards said fires broke out on three oil tankers that struck mines in the Strait of Hormuz.

10
00:00:57.099 --> 00:01:07.289
The Institute for the Study of War assesses those claims are likely meant to undermine ship operators' confidence in U.S. escort operations.

11
00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:08.108
Next, Saudi Arabia and Yemen.

12
00:01:08.108 --> 00:01:14.564
Reuters reports the Saudi led coalition intercepted missiles fired toward Riyadh and drones over the Eastern Province.

13
00:01:14.564 --> 00:01:28.952
The Long War Journal reports the Houthis are sustaining missile and drone attacks across Saudi Arabia, and the Institute for the Study of War says the Houthis also fired ballistic missiles at Yemeni government forces' staging areas and weapons depots in Lahij and Aden.

14
00:01:28.952 --> 00:01:31.509
Turning to Jordan.

15
00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:40.975
Reuters reports a Jordanian court sentenced three men to death over the deadly attack on a Greek Orthodox church in Karak on October twenty third.

16
00:01:40.975 --> 00:01:48.532
In Guatemala, Reuters reports the government decreed a state of emergency in two departments after a lawmaker was killed in an attack.

17
00:01:48.532 --> 00:01:53.951
D W reports the thirty day measure covers Zacapa and Izabal in the east of the country.

18
00:01:53.951 --> 00:01:55.316
And in Nigeria.

19
00:01:55.316 --> 00:02:08.715
A F P reports residents in Zamfara state say more than fifty people were killed on Thursday, November twelfth, when vigilantes from Zoma village in Bukkuyum district ambushed an armed gang returning from kidnappings in a neighboring district.

20
00:02:08.715 --> 00:02:12.925
A village chief put the dead at forty four bandits and nine vigilantes.

21
00:02:12.925 --> 00:02:15.554
Police said they had not yet received details.

22
00:02:15.554 --> 00:02:17.639
Now a few quick notes by region.

23
00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:23.320
In the Middle East, Reuters reports Hamas says a senior armed commander was killed in an Israeli strike.

24
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:28.579
The group's armed wing named him as Samir Abu Younis, commander of its Rafah brigade.

25
00:02:28.579 --> 00:02:44.485
In South Asia, Dawn reports Pakistan's military says security forces killed eight militants in Kolpur, Balochistan, and that on Saturday militants hit army patrol vehicles near Nushki with armed quadcopters, killing an army major and a non commissioned officer.

26
00:02:44.485 --> 00:03:00.932
In the Americas, an update on Friday's nationwide U.S. flight ground stop: Reuters reports Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said a contractor's work switching telecommunication lines from copper to fiber led to the longest nationwide shutdown of flights since the September eleventh attacks.

27
00:03:00.932 --> 00:03:09.680
And Australia's Smartraveller issued information for Australians in Illinois after an explosive device was found Friday at an ethanol plant in Peoria.

28
00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:15.325
The F B I says it is leading the investigation and that no additional suspicious devices were found.

29
00:03:15.325 --> 00:03:16.733
That's today's brief.

30
00:03:16.733 --> 00:03:24.933
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

31
00:03:24.933 --> 00:03:33.083
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

32
00:03:33.083 --> 00:03:35.167
This brief is digitally narrated.

33
00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.111
Questions?

34
00:03:36.111 --> 00:03:39.619
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

35
00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.651
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
